---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import '../styles/fileflex.css';
import '../styles/platform.css';
import '../styles/financial.css';
import '../styles/healthcare.css';

const blogs = [
  {
    title: 'HIPAA-Compliant File Sharing with Zero Trust: How to Secure PHI',
    blurb: 'HIPAA-compliant file sharing means adopting a robust security framework like Zero Trust Data Access (ZTDA) for guarding Protected Health Information (PHI) and…',
    img: '/images/healthcare/healthcard-blog-pic-e1686774963860-400x238.jpg',
    href: 'https://fileflex.com/blog/hippa-compliant-file-sharing/',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Healthcare — Protecting Access and Sharing of PHI with ZTDA for Windows | FileFlex"
  description="FileFlex Enterprise uses Zero Trust Data Access to protect, access, and share unstructured medical files and DICOM images across disparate healthcare silos — in compliance with HIPAA and GDPR."
>

<Nav />

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="hc-hero" aria-labelledby="hc-hero-heading">
  <div class="hc-hero__inner">
    <p class="hc-hero__eyebrow">HEALTHCARE</p>
    <h1 id="hc-hero-heading" class="hc-hero__title">
      Protecting Access and Sharing of Personal Health Information with ZTDA for Windows
    </h1>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     BLUE INTRO STRIP
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="hc-intro" aria-label="Overview">
  <div class="hc-intro__inner">
    <p class="hc-intro__text">
      Quality care means that unstructured medical files and DICOM images located in
      multiple disparate silos often need to be accessed and shared while protecting the
      privacy of personal health information (PHI) and in compliance with health and privacy
      regulations such as HIPAA. Secure sharing, which can be time-limited, is subject to
      user verification and can be micro-segmented down to file and folder level and access
      is granted only to the least privilege needed to complete the task &mdash; all within
      the secure framework of a ZTDA platform.
    </p>
    <p class="hc-intro__text">
      See also <strong><a href="https://fileflex.com/hipaa-compliance/">HIPAA Compliant File Sharing</a>.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     BODY — 3 image-left + text-right rows
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="fin-body" class="fin-body" aria-label="Healthcare use cases">
  <div class="fin-body__inner">

    <!-- Row 1 -->
    <div class="fin-block fin-row">
      <div class="fin-row__media">
        <img src="/images/healthcare/Screen-Shot-2022-12-12-at-2.03.27-PM-865x1024.jpg" alt="Compliant communication flow protecting patient privacy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="fin-row__copy">
        <h2 class="fin-h2">Improve Compliant Communication Flow While Protecting Patient Privacy</h2>
        <p class="fin-p">
          Patient care today involves multiple unrelated health providers &ndash; the family
          doctor, the specialist, the hospital, the clinic, labs, home care, physiotherapy,
          pharmacy, insurance, etc. FileFlex Enterprise allows personal health information
          (PHI) and DICOM images to be shared and accessed collaboratively and securely using
          ZTDA. And all actions are managed by IT, in compliance with health and privacy
          regulations such as HIPAA and GDPR.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="fin-sep" />

    <!-- Row 2 -->
    <div class="fin-block fin-row">
      <div class="fin-row__media">
        <img src="/images/healthcare/Screen-Shot-2022-12-12-at-2.03.18-PM-1024x811.jpg" alt="Secure data sharing between unrelated health providers" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="fin-row__copy">
        <h2 class="fin-h2">Secure Compliant Data Sharing Between Unrelated Health Providers</h2>
        <p class="fin-p">
          The location of unstructured data within the healthcare system can be incredibly
          complex. Not only can it be located in on-premises storage, but it could be with a
          cloud provider or on a SharePoint repository. Any of these can be used in the IT
          ecosystems of hospitals, clinics, independent labs, independent digital imaging
          providers, home care providers, physiotherapists, pharmacies, insurance agencies,
          etc. all operating as separate silos of information. The Zero Trust Data Access
          based platform of FileFlex Enterprise allows the many healthcare stakeholders
          access to each other&rsquo;s permitted healthcare information within Windows under
          a single-pane-of-glass where it can be accessed as if they were on a local drive,
          regardless of the difficulties related to the disparate systems and technologies.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="fin-sep" />

    <!-- Row 3 -->
    <div class="fin-block fin-row">
      <div class="fin-row__media">
        <img src="/images/healthcare/Screen-Shot-2022-12-12-at-2.03.36-PM-1024x992.jpg" alt="IT control over remote access to PHI" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="fin-row__copy">
        <h2 class="fin-h2">IT Control Over Remote Access to PHI</h2>
        <p class="fin-p">
          Governance and managing personal health information across disparate repository
          types, locations, and third parties can be a major problem. FileFlex Enterprise
          provides organizations with a management toolkit to control access to unstructured
          data which may include personal health information. It allows them to control data
          access, set policies, and assign access on a user-by-user or group-by-group basis
          with storage location, folder, or even file-level granularity. They have complete
          visibility to every action on every file or folder (including administrators)
          &ndash; whether it is access, modification or share &ndash; and gives management
          the ability to flag suspicious behavior.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     RELATED BLOG
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="fin-blogs" class="fin-section fin-section--white" aria-labelledby="hc-blogs-heading">
  <div class="fin-section__inner">
    <h2 id="hc-blogs-heading" class="fin-h2 fin-h2--center">Check Out This Related Blog</h2>
    <div class="fin-blog-grid hc-blog-grid">
      {blogs.map((b) => (
        <a class="fin-blog" href={b.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <img class="fin-blog__img" src={b.img} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="400" height="300" />
          <div class="fin-blog__body">
            <h3 class="fin-blog__title">{b.title}</h3>
            <p class="fin-blog__blurb">{b.blurb}</p>
            <span class="fin-blog__more">Read more →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
